> {[}(S, φ){]}/\(\mathcal{G}_{\text{sub}}\) --- they hold under the
> assumptions of the local spatial/gauge construction of §2.3 together
> with cubic-group representation theory, and under the conditions marked
> at each entry. These include, conditionally on H-link with its
> single-copy clause and H-cust (§4.5--§4.6): SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1) with
> multiplicities (3, 2, 1), three generations (chirality conditional on
> H-χ', §4.8) with identical gauge quantum numbers, one Higgs doublet (1,
> 2, +1/2), taken as input and accommodated in the E projection of the
> singlet taste (Theorem 11), unique hypercharges from anomaly
> cancellation (apart from the exceptional branch \(Y_Q=0\)), and the
> universal induced coupling \(1/\alpha_0 = 23.25\) (§6.1). These are
> theorems on the branch stated in §1 (Tier 2), with the conditions marked
> at each entry. The horizon calibration
> \(\hbar = c^3\epsilon^2/(4G\sigma)\) and the Bekenstein-Hawking
> coefficient it matches hold for the same class as consistency relations
> conditional on H-count, which includes finiteness of the total system
> and a conserved energy shell, and on H-slope, H-frame, the horizon and
> frame conditions, local boost structure and the symmetric
> detailed-balance rate ratio ({[}GR §2.3, §3.2, §4--§5, §8.5{]}). They do
> not depend on which specific φ describes our universe.
